  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "## 12.2.3\n\n### Fixes\n- Character formatting set on a nested inline is no longer overwritten by the outer one when writing. RTF character formatting is a flat attribute set, so the writer resolves the inline hierarchy itself - and it merged the two the wrong way round, letting an ancestor's value win over the value on the inline that actually carries it. A font size applied over a selection that spans several paragraphs was written out as the old size for any paragraph whose whole content sits inside a bold, italic or underline element: applying the value there lands on the wrapping element, under a span that still carries the previous size, so the document kept rendering the new size while a save emitted the old one and reloading lost the change. The same inversion affected every character property (font family, colours, letter spacing) and superscript/subscript on nested inlines.",
